{% if v.turbo %}

### Turbo Frame

Wrap content that should be replaced independently of the rest of the page:

```erb
<%= turbo_frame_tag "profile_#{@profile.id}" do %>
  <%= render {% if v.vc %}(ProfileCardComponent.new(profile: @profile)){% elif v.phlex %}Components::ProfileCard.new(profile: @profile){% else %}"profiles/card", profile: @profile{% endif %} %>
  <%= link_to "Edit", edit_profile_path(@profile) %>
<% end %>
```

The edit page renders the matching frame, and Turbo swaps it in:

```erb
<!-- app/views/profiles/edit.html.erb -->
<%= turbo_frame_tag "profile_#{@profile.id}" do %>
  <%= render "form", profile: @profile %>
<% end %>
```

### Turbo Stream

Broadcast updates from controllers or models:

```ruby
# In a controller
def create
  @comment = @post.comments.create!(comment_params)
  respond_to do |format|
    format.turbo_stream # renders create.turbo_stream.erb
    format.html { redirect_to @post }
  end
end
```

```erb
<!-- app/views/comments/create.turbo_stream.erb -->
<%= turbo_stream.append "comments", partial: "comments/comment", locals: { comment: @comment } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "new_comment_form", partial: "comments/form", locals: { comment: Comment.new } %>
```
{% endif %}
{% if v.stim %}

### Stimulus Controller

`app/javascript/controllers/dropdown_controller.js`:

```js
import { Controller } from "@hotwired/stimulus"

export default class extends Controller {
  static targets = ["menu"]
  static values = { open: Boolean }

  connect() {
    this.close = this.close.bind(this)
  }

  toggle(event) {
    event.preventDefault()
    this.openValue = !this.openValue
  }

  openValueChanged(open) {
{% if v.ui == 'tailwind' %}
    this.menuTarget.classList.toggle("hidden", !open)
{% elif v.ui == 'bootstrap' %}
    this.menuTarget.classList.toggle("show", open)
{% else %}
    this.menuTarget.hidden = !open
{% endif %}
    if (open) {
      document.addEventListener("click", this.close)
    } else {
      document.removeEventListener("click", this.close)
    }
  }

  close(event) {
    if (this.element.contains(event.target)) return
    this.openValue = false
  }
}
```

Use it in HTML:

```erb
<div data-controller="dropdown" data-dropdown-open-value="false" class="{{ v.css.dropdown }}">
  <button data-action="dropdown#toggle" class="{{ v.css.button }}">
    Options
  </button>
  <div data-dropdown-target="menu" class="{{ v.css.menu }}"{% if v.ui == 'none' %} hidden{% endif %}>
    <%= link_to "Edit", edit_path, class: "{{ v.css.menu_item }}" %>
  </div>
</div>
```
{% endif %}

### Form{{ ' (Turbo-aware)' if v.turbo else '' }}

```erb
<%= form_with(model: @profile, class: "{{ v.css.form }}") do |form| %>
  <% if @profile.errors.any? %>
    <div class="{{ v.css.errors }}" role="alert">
      <ul class="{{ v.css.errors_list }}">
        <% @profile.errors.full_messages.each do |msg| %>
          <li><%= msg %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div>
    <%= form.label :name, class: "{{ v.css.label }}" %>
    <%= form.text_field :name, class: "{{ v.css.input }}" %>
  </div>

  <%= form.submit class: "{{ v.css.button }}" %>
<% end %>
```

The controller MUST render with `status: :unprocessable_entity` on validation
failure{% if v.turbo %} or Turbo will not re-render the form{% endif %}.

## Style Rules (MANDATORY)

{% if v.vc %}
- **`frozen_string_literal: true`** on every Ruby component file
- **ApplicationComponent base** — all components inherit from it
- **Keyword args** in `initialize`
- **Private `attr_reader`** for instance variables
- **No DB queries in components or helpers** — pass data in via `initialize`
- **Sidecar templates** (`.html.erb` next to `.rb`) for components with markup
{% elif v.phlex %}
- **`frozen_string_literal: true`** on every Ruby component file
- **`Components::Base`** — all components inherit from it, namespaced under `Components::`
- **Keyword args** in `initialize`
- **Markup in `view_template`**, class-name logic in private methods
- **No DB queries in components or helpers** — pass data in via `initialize`
- **No `unsafe_raw`** unless the HTML is trusted and sanitized
{% else %}
- **Partials declare their locals** with `<%# locals: (...) %>`
- **Partials receive data via `locals:`** — never read controller instance variables
- **Shared partials** live in `app/views/shared/`
- **No DB queries in views, partials or helpers** — the controller loads the data
{% endif %}
- **`t('...')` for all user-visible strings** — never hardcode English
{% if v.ui == 'tailwind' %}
- **Tailwind classes grouped** — layout → spacing → typography → color → state
{% elif v.ui == 'bootstrap' %}
- **Bootstrap components and utilities first** — custom CSS only when no utility fits
{% else %}
- **Semantic class names** (BEM) with styles in `app/assets/stylesheets/` — no inline `style=`
{% endif %}
{% if v.stim %}
- **Stimulus controllers small and focused** — one responsibility each
- **No inline JavaScript** — always a Stimulus controller
{% else %}
- **No JavaScript** — no inline handlers, no `<script>` tags
{% endif %}
- **Forms use `form_with`** (NOT `form_for` or `form_tag`)
- **Buttons use `button_to` for state-changing actions** (proper HTTP method + CSRF)
- **Always provide `alt` text** on images
- **Always provide labels** on form fields (visible or {% if v.ui == 'bootstrap' %}`visually-hidden`{% elif v.ui == 'tailwind' %}`sr-only`{% else %}a visually-hidden class{% endif %})
{% if v.vc or v.phlex %}

## Component vs Partial — when to use which

| Use a {{ variables.component_library }} component when | Use a partial when |
|--------------------------|---------------------|
| The same UI appears in 3+ places | The UI is rendered once or twice |
| There is non-trivial logic to compute classes/values | The markup is straightforward |
| The component has variants (size, color, state) | No variants |
| You want unit tests on the component | Spec is covered by system spec |
| Slots are needed (header/body/footer pattern) | A flat parameter list is enough |
{% endif %}

